  "raw": {
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Director-of-Development_R1027-1": {
      "title": "Director of Development",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  Job Summary The Director of Development serves as a strategic fundraising leader responsible for advancing philanthropic support for the Cotsakos College of Business and the Honors College. This role partners closely with academic leadership to translate institutional priorities into compelling donor opportunities and drives major gift fundraising through relationship-building, strategic planning, and cross-functional collaboration. This role reports to the Vice President of Institutional Advancement. Core Competencies & Skills Strategic Fundraising & Revenue Generation Demonstrates advanced ability to design and execute comprehensive fundraising strategies aligned with institutional and academic priorities. Proven success in cultivating, soliciting, and closing major and principal gifts ($25K+). Ability to translate academic initiatives (scholarships, faculty support, innovation, student success) into compelling donor investment opportunities. Experience contributing to and advancing comprehensive fundraising campaigns and long-term revenue goals. Relationship Management & Donor Engagement Exceptional skill in building, managing, and deepening relationships with high-net-worth individuals, alumni, corporate leaders, foundations, and community stakeholders. Ability to develop trust-based, long-term partnerships that result in sustained philanthropic support. Demonstrated ability to engage diverse stakeholders, including faculty, administrators, volunteers, and advisory boards. Strong interpersonal skills with cultural competence and emotional intelligence. Leadership & Strategic Partnership Development Ability to serve as a trusted advisor and primary liaison to academic leadership, including Deans and senior administrators. Demonstrated success aligning fundraising initiatives with academic vision and institutional priorities. Skilled at influencing and collaborating across departments without direct authority. Ability to engage and mobilize volunteers, advisory boards, and leadership prospects in advancement efforts. Corporate, Foundation & Alumni Engagement Knowledge of corporate and foundation relations, including grant development, sponsorships, and partnership cultivation. Ability to identify and secure strategic partnerships that enhance institutional visibility and financial support. Experience leveraging alumni networks, events, and engagement initiatives to strengthen donor pipelines. Communication & Proposal Development Advanced written and verbal communication skills, including persuasive storytelling and case development. Ability to create compelling proposals, presentations, stewardship reports, and donor communications. Skilled at tailoring messaging for diverse audiences (individual, corporate, foundation). Portfolio & Data Management Proven ability to manage a portfolio of major gift prospects using data-driven strategies. Experience utilizing CRM systems (e.g., Banner, Raiser’s Edge, Salesforce) to track activity, manage pipelines, and forecast revenue. Strong analytical skills to assess donor capacity, engagement, and strategy effectiveness. Project Management & Execution Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines, and complex initiatives simultaneously. Strong planning and execution skills in support of events, campaigns, and donor engagement strategies. Ability to work independently while maintaining alignment with broader advancement goals. Professionalism, Ethics & Stewardship Demonstrates integrity, discretion, and adherence to ethical fundraising standards and confidentiality. Commitment to best practices in donor stewardship and institutional compliance. Exercises sound judgment, initiative, and accountability in managing donor relationships and institutional resources. General Job Duties Manage a portfolio of 100–125 major gift prospects, leading identification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship efforts. Serve as the primary development liaison to the Deans of the Cotsakos College of Business and the Honors College. Develop and implement fundraising strategies supporting scholarships, faculty excellence, experiential learning, and innovation initiatives. Collaborate with academic leadership, advancement teams, and external stakeholders to identify and advance funding opportunities. Build and maintain relationships with alumni, parents, corporations, foundations, and community leaders. Partner with Corporate and Foundation Relations and Alumni Engagement teams on donor strategy and outreach. Prepare proposals, stewardship reports, and donor communications aligned with institutional priorities. Support campaign planning, pipeline development, and fundraising goal achievement. Maintain accurate donor records and activity tracking within CRM systems. Represent the institution at events and engagement opportunities. Ensure compliance with ethical fundraising practices and institutional policies. Perform additional duties in support of advancement initiatives as assigned. Education and Experience Minimum Required Bachelor’s degree required; advanced degree preferred. Minimum 5–7 years of progressive fundraising experience, preferably in higher education or nonprofit environments. Demonstrated success in major gift fundraising and donor relationship management. Experience working with academic leadership, corporate partners, alumni, foundations, and volunteer boards preferred. Proven ability to manage complex stakeholder environments and contribute to strategic initiatives. This description indicates the general nature and level of work performed by employees in the above job. It is not intended to be a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of employees assigned to the job. Salary - NAL - $100,000 - $110,002 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:  Benefits Package Pamphlet (NAL) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact: humanresources@wpunj.edu  . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Professor--Computer-Science_R1066": {
      "title": "Professor, Computer Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  Job Summary William Paterson University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Associate or Full Professor in the Department of Computer Science, with an anticipated appointment as Department Chair. We seek an accomplished scholar and academic leader to advance the Department’s computer science, information technology, and cybersecurity programs. The appointment will begin in July 2027. The search will prioritize candidates with expertise in data science; artificial intelligence and cybersecurity; cloud and network security; digital forensics; privacy and data security; secure systems; and emerging cyber threats. Candidates with expertise in related areas are also encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will provide strategic leadership in teaching, research, experiential learning, and external partnerships, while advancing innovative methodologies, technologies, and applications that address critical real-world challenges. Department Chair Opportunity The Department Chair provides academic and administrative leadership for the Computer Science Department. Responsibilities include managing departmental budgets and course scheduling; supporting admissions, accreditation, assessment, and faculty recruitment; implementing university and college policies; and advancing the Department’s academic programs and strategic priorities. The Chair works closely with students, faculty, the Dean of the College of Science and Health, and university units to promote student success, address academic concerns, advocate for the Department, and strengthen its programs and operations. Reassigned time from teaching is provided for Chair responsibilities. Department Overview The Computer Science Department’s programs are informed by ACM/IEEE undergraduate curriculum guidelines. The Department offers B.S. and M.S. degrees in Computer Science and a B.S. in Information Technology (IT) with an IT-Cybersecurity track. The B.S. in Information Technology is offered both on campus and online. The Department prepares students for graduate study and professional careers in software development, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, data science, and related areas. Its growing strengths in cybersecurity education and research are supported by specialized research and instructional facilities, student activities and competitions, and expanding online offerings. The B.S. in Computer Science is ABET-accredited. Multidisciplinary research and exceptional teaching within a highly diverse and inclusive campus community are central to the University’s mission. Computer Science faculty are highly collaborative and engaged in cutting-edge, interdisciplinary research. Reporting Relationship The Department Chair reports to the Dean of the College of Science and Health. Duties and Responsibilities Provide academic and strategic leadership for the Computer Science Department in collaboration with faculty, the Dean, and university leadership. Lead the continued development and expansion of the Department’s cybersecurity academic programs, research initiatives, experiential learning opportunities, and external partnerships. Provide leadership for accreditation, assessment, and continuous improvement, including maintaining ABET accreditation of the B.S. in Computer Science. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in multiple modalities, including online instruction. While serving as Department Chair, teach at least one course per semester. Lead curriculum and program development, including course content, learning objectives, assessment, and continuous improvement. Promote student success through effective advising, mentoring, curriculum development, and program management. Maintain an active and productive record of scholarship and publication. Participate in departmental, college, and university committees and activities that advance academic programs and university priorities. Perform other teaching and administrative responsibilities as assigned based on departmental needs. Required Qualifications Earned doctorate in Computer Science or a closely related field. Demonstrated academic leadership and the ability to lead collaboratively in a complex university environment. Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Demonstrated scholarly productivity appropriate for appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor. Demonstrated expertise and a record of scholarship, teaching, or professional activity in cybersecurity or a closely related area. Preferred Qualifications Prior academic administrative leadership experience, such as department chair, program director, or comparable leadership in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related discipline. Knowledge of and experience with ABET accreditation standards and processes. Experience securing or maintaining an NSA National Center of Academic Excellence (CAE) designation in cybersecurity, or comparable cybersecurity program development experience. Experience developing, expanding, or leading cybersecurity academic programs, curricula, laboratories, centers, or related initiatives.. Leadership Attributes Demonstrated ability to lead, collaborate with, and influence faculty and colleagues in a complex and diverse academic environment. Ability to identify priorities, build consensus, and advance departmental and institutional goals. Commitment to student success, academic excellence, innovation, and inclusive excellence. Exceptional communication, interpersonal, and relationship-building skills, with the ability to build consensus, navigate competing priorities, advocate effectively for the Department, and develop productive partnerships with internal and external stakeholders. Starting Salary - AFT Range 32 - $113,015 - $129,973 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:  Benefits Package Pamphlet (AFT Faculty) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact: h umanresources@wpunj.edu Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Associate-Dean--School-of-Nursing_R1065": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, School of Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.    Job Summary Reporting to the Dean, College of Science and Health, the Associate Dean, School of Nursing, collaborates with the Dean of the College of Science and Health and the Chairperson to provide leadership and vision for the development, growth, quality, and continuous improvement of the School’s academic programs. The Associate Dean provides leadership for accreditation and regulatory compliance, student success and progression, clinical education and healthcare partnerships, faculty and staff development, and strategic planning. The position establishes and maintains effective partnerships with healthcare providers to ensure high-quality clinical experiences, support workforce-aligned curriculum development, strengthen student outcomes, and advance the School’s accreditation and strategic priorities. Major Duties and Responsibilities Ensures quality for the School of Nursing programs by working with the Chair and faculty to maintain professional accreditation with CCNE, New Jersey Board of Nursing, and other relevant agencies; Oversees preparation, submission, and correspondence related to accreditation and re-accreditation of the baccalaureate, masters, and doctoral nursing programs, including, but not limited to: Self-study for all programs to the CCNE, Self-study to the NJ Board of Nursing of the undergraduate pre-licensure programs, Continuous Improvement Reports (CIPR), and Substantive change reports to CCNE. Represents the School of Nursing when serving on internal and external councils and committees and attending functions. Assists in identifying external members for the Nursing Advisory Committee; organizes and chairs meetings of the Nursing Advisory Committee at least twice a year. Actively pursues grants and outside funding sources for major projects, research, curriculum enhancement, and equipment. Participates in the implementation/revision of University, College, & School of Nursing Strategic Plans and maintains a Strategic Plan for the School of Nursing. Engages with the Office of Institutional Effectiveness, Registrar, and other appropriate offices to develop and receive relevant program data, reports, and schedules; monitors nursing data for alignment with the Key Performance Indicators of the University. Recommends and monitors nursing program budgets in Collaboration with the Dean of COSH. Collaborates with the Chairperson to recommend to the Dean the reappointments of qualified nursing staff as related to professional development. Collaborates with the Chairperson to assess the effectiveness of nursing student admissions processes and provides recommendations for improvement. Establishes and monitors academic standards for all nursing programs in Collaboration with the faculty. Assists in the resolution of student complaints or issues concerning academic standards, instruction, grades, and program requirements. Serves as a custodian of all academic integrity violation records for Nursing students. Represents School of Nursing on the university’s Students of Concern Committee. Represents the School of Nursing on open houses, accepted students’ day, and new student orientations. Provides and monitors the effectiveness of orientation programs for new full-time, part-time, and adjunct nursing faculty and non-tenure track teaching professionals. Maintains currency of knowledge in nursing by attending state and national meetings of nursing educators and administrators. Encourages and supports articulation with community colleges when appropriate. Serves as liaison between faculty and offices such as Registrar, Admissions, Student Accounts, and Student Enrollment Services. Supervises professional staff assigned to the nursing programs. Performs other duties as assigned and appropriate for the position. Education and Experience Terminal Degree in nursing, such as PhD, Ed. D or DNP in Nursing New Jersey Nursing licensure or ability to gain licensure within 6 (six) months of onboarding Minimum of five years of experience in academic nursing programs    Competencies/Skills Required Strong understanding of nursing education and administration Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills Exhibits initiative, enthusiasm, and teamwork in accomplishing responsibilities Fosters a departmental climate that supports collegiality and professional development of students, faculty, and staff   This description indicates the general nature and level of work performed by employees in the above job. It is not intended to be a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of employees assigned to the job. Salary - NAL - $139,717 - $165,222 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit: Benefits Package Pamphlet (NAL) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact: humanresources@wpunj.edu . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Nursing-Student-Success-Coordinator_R1054": {
      "title": "Nursing Student Success Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  JOB SUMMARY Reporting to the Associate Dean, School of Nursing, the Student Success Coordinator manages the Nursing Enrichment and Tutoring Center (NET), coordinates scheduling of tutors and mentors, facilitates management of undergraduate and graduate cohorts, identification and management of academically at-risk students. Note: Bachelor’s Degree in Nursing required/Master’s degree in Nursing Education preferred. PRINCIPAL RESPONSIBILITIES Manages the day to day operations of the Nursing Enrichment and Tutoring (NET) Center Works closely with the undergraduate and graduate level coordinators to ensure at-risk students are identified and receive ongoing tutoring and support Works closely with the Skills/Sim lab coordinator to ensure students have opportunity to practice necessary skills in the NET Manages any supplemental instructional offerings in conjunction with the COSH requirements In conjunction with the Associate Dean, evaluates NCLEX pass rates as well as Certificate pass rates to ensure curricular alignment and program offerings as needed Serves on the Curriculum Committee as well as the Academic Standards Committee to ensure alignment of services at the undergraduate and graduate levels Hires, orients, trains, and supervises nursing student tutors and mentors as appropriate Develops and recommends an appropriate budget for all activities supervised Gathers and reviews data on student response to NET activities each semester and initiates new programs as indicated Assesses undergraduate and graduate retention issues and plans interventions accordingly Serves as a resource to the Student Nurses Association Implements special projects as requested by the Associate Dean and the Chairperson i.e. assist with the arrangements for the Nursing Community Advisory Board (CAB) Directs academic support and referrals for undergraduate and graduate nursing students Provides or arranges for workshops to enhance student success for undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral nursing students Performs other duties as assigned that are appropriate for the position MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s Degree in Nursing required/Master’s degree in Nursing Education preferred Minimum 2 years experience in mentoring/tutoring/advising students Knowledge of Microsoft Office and familiarity with audiovisual equipment Experience with Nursing Simulation Excellent written and oral communication skills; strong presentation skills Flexibility to work occasional evenings and weekends, as needed This description indicates the general nature and level of work performed by employees in the above job. It is not intended to be a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of employees assigned to the job. Starting Salary - AFT Range 24 - $76,486.40 - $87,954.55 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:  BENEFITS FOR PROFESSIONAL STAFF (AFT) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact  h umanresources@wpunj.edu . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
