    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Associate-Director-of-Corporate---Foundation-Relations_R1031": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Corporate & Foundation Relations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  Position Summary The Associate Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations supports the university’s institutional fundraising efforts by managing foundation relations activities, coordinating grant development processes, and supporting strategic partnerships with institutional funders. This position works closely with the Office of Sponsored Programs, faculty, deans, and university leadership to identify foundation funding opportunities, support proposal development, and ensure effective stewardship and reporting for foundation grants and philanthropic investments. The Associate Director plays a key role in strengthening the university’s foundation fundraising pipeline and supporting collaborative funding strategies across the institution. This role reports to the Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations. Key Duties and Responsibilities Foundation Relations & Grant Support Assist in implementing the university’s foundation relations strategy in alignment with institutional priorities. Manage a portfolio of foundation prospects and donors with emphasis on cultivation, stewardship, proposal coordination, and relationship management. Research and identify new private and family foundation funding opportunities. Coordinate and support the preparation of letters of inquiry, grant proposals, reports, and stewardship communications. Collaboration with Office of Sponsored Programs Serve as a primary liaison between Institutional Advancement and the Office of Sponsored Programs for foundation-related opportunities. Collaborate with faculty and staff to identify funding opportunities that align with academic, research, and programmatic priorities. Assist in coordinating institutional review and submission processes for foundation proposals. Support compliance with proposal requirements, grant reporting deadlines, and stewardship expectations. Proposal Development & Stewardship Draft and edit compelling narratives, cases for support, grant reports, and donor communications. Coordinate proposal timelines, supporting documentation, budgets, and submission materials. Assist in developing stewardship strategies to ensure continued engagement and long-term support from foundation funders. Support campus visits, funder meetings, and donor recognition activities. Prospect Research & Portfolio Management Conduct prospect research and maintain detailed records within the university’s CRM system. Track deadlines, proposal activity, and funding outcomes. Monitor trends in foundation philanthropy and share relevant opportunities with university stakeholders. Administrative & Team Support Support the Manager of Corporate and Foundation Relations in achieving departmental fundraising goals and strategic priorities. Assist with data management, reporting, and departmental communications. Participate in university advancement and donor engagement activities as needed Perform other duties in support of advancement initiatives and institutional goals. Education and Experience Minimum Required Bachelor’s degree. Minimum of 2–4 years of experience in foundation relations, grant writing, sponsored programs, fundraising, nonprofit development, or related work. Strong writing, editing, organizational, and project management skills. Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines in a collaborative environment. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Experience conducting research and preparing funding proposals or reports. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and CRM/database systems.  Preferred Experience working in higher education, sponsored programs, research administration, or nonprofit development. Familiarity with foundation grant processes and proposal development. Experience coordinating with faculty, researchers, or academic leadership. Knowledge of institutional fundraising and donor stewardship practices. This description indicates the general nature and level of work performed by employees in the above job. It is not intended to be a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of employees assigned to the job. Salary - NAL - $ 66,826.62 - $ 80,191.94 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:  Benefits Package Pamphlet (NAL) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact: humanresources@wpunj.edu  . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department.   Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Director-Internal-Audit_R1045": {
      "title": "Director Internal Audit",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  Job Summary: Reporting with dotted line responsibility to the President and Vice President for Finance and Administration and solid line responsibility to the Board of Trustees, the Director of Internal Audit assesses organizational, compliance and operational risks, based on the development of an annual audit plan supplemented by departmental audits and the risk assessment.  The Director provides independent and objective risk assessment of the operation and effectiveness of internal controls, processes and procedures in academic as well as administrative offices and departments. They also provide support to University’s external auditors in the conduct of annual Financial Statement audits. The Director also serves as the University’s Conscientious Employee Protection Act (CEPA) Officer, investigates, and reports on issues to the University President and Board of Trustees, as appropriate or necessary. The Director of Internal Audit is administratively part of the Office of General Counsel. Responsibilities include: Schedules, prepares, and conducts internal audits in accordance with standards promulgated by the Institute of Internal Auditors; evaluates University internal controls and the control environment. Evaluates the effectiveness and efficiency of operations, the reliability of financial reporting mechanisms, and institutional compliance with applicable laws and regulations. Prepares annual internal audit/risk assessment schedule based on internal audit standards for detailed reviews of academic and administrative offices and departments. Conducts pre-audit meetings with department heads prior to the start of every audit, as well as exit meetings.  Reviews audit findings with department heads at the conclusion of each audit and consults, as needed, to determine any remedial action needed.  Prepares formal audit reports, which detail audit findings, recommendations for corrective actions, and management responses for the audit committee of the University.  In addition, follows up with unit to ensure corrective actions or remedial steps have been completed and implemented. Develops and recommends policies, procedures, practices, and systems designed to enhance internal controls; communicates same to the department head, Senior Administration, and the Finance, Audit, and Institutional Development Committee of the Board of Trustees (University’s audit committee). Prepares the quarterly Recommendation Follow-up Matrix for all completed audit and tracks corrective actions taken for all audit recommendations. Completes, documents and issues formal report on special projects as assigned. Serves as the University’s Conscientious Employee Protection Act (CEPA) officer; receives and reviews complaints while maintaining strict confidentiality. Assesses the veracity of CEPA complaints, conducts investigations as appropriate or necessary, and reports findings to the President; updates the Finance, Audit and Institutional Development Committee of the Board of Trustees on the status of CEPA reviews on a quarterly basis. Performs other duties as assigned that are appropriate for the position. Minimum qualifications include: Bachelor’s Degree in Accounting, Management Information Systems, Business or related field, with major course work/emphasis in Accounting and or Finance MBA, CPA or other relevant advanced education preferred. CPA, CISA or CIA certification preferred.  Ten (10) years of relevant professional experience in progressively responsible positions within a public or private college or university, state or federal agency, accounting/auditing firm or corporation. Extensive knowledge of the principles and practices of accounting and internal auditing is required, as is the thorough understanding of corporate and/or public higher education compliance programs. Working knowledge of the COSO Internal Control Framework and OMB Uniform Guidance for federal grants preferred Strong critical thinking skills and the ability to analyze, research, summarize and effectively present information. Ability to work independently in a highly confidential environment. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Excellent computer skills with advanced knowledge of Microsoft Office, and Workday a plus. High ethical standards and values are required, as are excellent leadership and management skills and the ability to organize, prioritize and multi-task. This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:   Benefits Package Pamphlet (NAL) Salary - NAL - $101,860 - $149,972 Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact: humanresources@wpunj.edu   . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Associate-Director--Student-Accounts_R1020": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Student Accounts",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  JOB SUMMARY Under the leadership of the Director of Student Accounts, the Associate Director assists in the overall management and administration of the Office of Student Accounts, including billing, receivables, collections, cashiering, payment processing, refunds, tax reporting, and related technologies. The Associate Director is responsible for the day-to-day supervision of the Collections, Customer Service, and Cash Processing units, consisting of five staff members, and ensures the efficient and effective operation of each functional area. The Associate Director shares responsibility for maintaining Banner fee assessment rules, student refunds, and payment processing systems while ensuring compliance with applicable federal, state, and University policies. The position assists in the development and implementation of operational improvements, oversees critical technology resources including Banner and TouchNet, and works collaboratively with campus partners to improve student financial services and operational efficiency. PRINCIPAL RESPONSIBILITIES Assists in the overall management and administration of the Office of Student Accounts by supporting departmental planning, implementing operational improvements, establishing internal controls, and ensuring compliance with University policies and applicable federal and state regulations. Administers and maintains Banner Student Accounts and related technologies, including TouchNet and other student financial systems. Coordinates system testing, validates upgrades, investigates system issues, recommends enhancements, and assists with implementation of new technologies and business processes. Oversees the University's tuition and fee assessment processes, including Banner billing rules, detail codes, tuition structures, and fee assessment for Main Campus, WP Online, High School, and other specialized student populations. Ensures data integrity and accuracy of student billing. Manages student refund and payment processing operations, including Banner auto-refunds, TouchNet refund files, direct deposit, paper check processing, payment plans, credit card refunds, Marketplace/uPay administration, user access, and related payment technologies. Performs and oversees financial reconciliations related to student accounts, financial aid, bookstore deferments, payment processing, and other accounts receivable activities. Investigates and resolves discrepancies and prepares adjusting and closing journal entries as required. Coordinates regulatory reporting and compliance activities, including annual IRS Form 1098-T reporting, Nursing Faculty Loan Program reporting, and other required federal, state, and institutional reporting requirements. Develops, analyzes, and distributes operational, financial, collection, and management reports to support departmental operations, strategic planning, decision-making, and compliance requirements. Assists with internal and external audits by preparing work papers, responding to auditor inquiries, providing supporting documentation, and implementing recommendations as appropriate. Supervises the daily operations of the Collections, Customer Service, and Cash Processing units, including assigning work, establishing schedules, approving leave, monitoring productivity, evaluating performance, coaching staff, and ensuring appropriate office coverage. Provides leadership and guidance to staff by fostering collaboration, accountability, customer service excellence, professional development, and continuous process improvement while promoting a positive and inclusive work environment. Interprets and applies University policies and procedures related to student accounts, billing, collections, payment plans, tuition refunds, and other financial processes. Resolves complex student account issues requiring independent judgment and managerial decision-making. Serves as a primary liaison with Financial Aid, Business Services, Information Technology, the Registrar, Residence Life, Admissions, auditors, vendors, banking partners, and other internal and external stakeholders to coordinate student financial operations and improve cross-functional processes. Assists the Director in developing departmental policies, procedures, strategic initiatives, and operational goals designed to improve efficiency, strengthen internal controls, enhance customer service, and support the University's strategic objectives. Represents the Office of Student Accounts and the University on committees, professional organizations, conferences, training programs, and other meetings as assigned. Performs other duties as assigned that are appropriate to the scope and responsibilities of the position. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, Higher Education Administration, or a related field. Five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in student accounts, bursar operations, accounts receivable, or higher education finance, including at least two (2) years of supervisory experience. Experience with student financial systems and student account operations, including billing, receivables, collections, payment processing, and refunds. Knowledge of applicable federal and state regulations, accounting principles, internal controls, and student account compliance requirements. Strong leadership, analytical, organizational, communication, and customer service skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master's degree in a related field. Experience working in a public college or university. Experience with Ellucian Banner Student Accounts and TouchNet. Experience managing Banner fee assessment, tuition structures, 1098-T reporting, or other complex student account system administration. Experience leading system implementations, process improvements, or major technology initiatives. Salary - NAL - $82,500 - $128,800 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:   Benefits Package Pamphlet (NAL) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact: humanresources@wpunj.edu   . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Associate-Registrar_R1022-1": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-06\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  Job Summary Reporting to the Registrar, the Associate Registrar provides operational leadership for core functions that support the mission of the Registrar’s Office and the institution. The role focuses on ensuring effective, compliant, and student‑centered operations while anticipating and responding to changes in enrollment patterns, academic programming, and institutional priorities. The Associate Registrar demonstrates forward‑thinking leadership by evaluating and improving processes, aligning resources and workflows across the office, and identifying opportunities to enhance service delivery, efficiency, and consistency in support of academic and student success goals. This position provides high‑level strategic direction for a wide range of departmental operations and delivers internal and external training, along with comprehensive documentation for policies and procedures. Principal Responsibilities Provide strategic oversight of academic systems and catalog operations, including Banner, Degree Works, and Banner Workflow; serve as senior backup and ensure accurate, timely updates aligned with academic policy and new certificate and degree program development. Lead the continuous improvement of registrar systems, workflows, and business processes to support scalable, efficient operations across all campuses and modalities. Partner with academic leadership, administrative units, and campus stakeholders to guide the planning, launch, and operational integration of certificate and emerging academic programs, ensuring compliance and smooth execution. Direct operational planning to support enrollment growth, including onboarding new programs, aligning registrar services with student needs, and proactively addressing process and capacity requirements. Manage and supervise staff responsible for core student record services (transfer credit evaluation, enrollment verification, transcripts, degree and certificate audits), providing senior‑level systems analysis, project management, and process redesign to enhance service quality and user experience. Serve as the institutional data steward for student academic records, ensuring data integrity, regulatory compliance, and timely, effective response to internal and external reporting needs. Oversee the clear and consistent communication of academic policies, procedures, and student rights, maintaining accurate and accessible information across all platforms. Represent the Office of Registration Services and the University Registrar on committees, working groups, and institutional initiatives, contributing subject‑matter expertise and leadership on special projects. Ensure compliance with FERPA, federal and New Jersey regulations, and University policies while fostering a collaborative, service‑oriented, and learning‑focused work environment. Provide operational leadership for the Registrar’s Office in the absence of the University Registrar and perform additional managerial duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in a field related to the position. 5 years of related work experience in an Enrollment Management Office in higher education, experience working in the area of registrar or registration services preferred. Strong knowledge of FERPA and student related compliance reporting. Proficiency with MS Office software and student information systems (e.g., Banner). Demonstrated understanding of complex databases and computer systems researching and collecting data. Possess critical thinking and interpretive skills to analyze situations, define problems, interpret policies, identify concerns, develop and propose solutions. Ability to work collaboratively with others, and high degree of professionalism required. Demonstrated strong organizational, analytical, written, verbal communication and presentation skills. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, and problem-solving skills. This description indicates the general nature and level of work performed by employees in the above job. It is not intended to be a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of employees assigned to the job. Salary - NAL - $74,251 - $111,000 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:   Benefits Package Pamphlet (NAL) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact: humanresources@wpunj.edu   . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Assistant-Director---Office-of-Field-Experiences---Partnerships_R1019": {
      "title": "Assistant Director - Office of Field Experiences & Partnerships",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-26\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  Job Summary Reporting to the Director of the Office of Field Experiences and Partnerships, the Assistant Director for the Office of Field Experiences and Partnerships supports the planning, implementation, and continuous improvement of clinical experiences and school-university partnerships within William Paterson University's College of Education. Working collaboratively with faculty, P–12 school partners, clinical supervisors, and Professors in Residence, the Assistant Director helps ensure high-quality field experiences that prepare educator candidates for success in diverse educational settings. Key responsibilities include assisting with the management of clinical placement processes, collecting and analyzing program data, supporting accreditation and reporting efforts, facilitating alternate route clinical procedures, conducting candidate data audits to ensure clinical readiness, coordinating recruitment and onboarding of clinical supervisors and Professors in Residence, and serving as a primary point of communication for candidates and school partners. The Assistant Director also leads the Aspiring Educators Summer Program and contributes to the development and sustainability of innovative school-university partnerships that strengthen educator preparation and advance student success. Department Overview The Office of Field Experiences and Partnerships develops and supports School-University Partnerships and implements quality clinical experiences in the context of documented and effective partnerships with P-12 schools and districts through a long-standing, extensive professional development school network, input from P-12 schools and districts through the School-University Partnership Advisory Council, extensive and scaffolded initial teacher licensure candidate experience in diverse clinical settings, clinical assessment of traditional, alternate route, and advanced licensure candidates in diverse clinical settings, and enactment of a system that relies upon quality sites with selected and prepared clinical educators, experienced and trained clinical supervisors, and highly supported clinical candidates.    College Overview Join the distinguished College of Education where excellence is reflected in our mission and vision. Our AAQEP-accredited initial and advanced educator preparation programs reflect best practices and align with state, national, and professional association standards. Our staff and faculty recognize the diverse strengths and challenges of our students and are actively engaged in their success.  Duties and Responsibilities: Assist in the management and oversight of the Office of Field Experiences and Partnerships.  Engage in data collection, analysis, and reporting Engage in clinical and professional development school and school-university partnership activities and programs Engage in clinical supervisor and professor in residence recruitment, onboarding and support Engage in communications with candidates, faculty, clinical supervisors, professors in residence to field questions and share information. Facilitate the alternate route programs clinical processes and procedures. Ensure candidate clinical preparedness through data audits. Lead and implement the Aspiring Educators Summer Program Required Qualifications: An earned bachelor’s degree in education or related field, master’s degree preferred Minimum of five years teaching experience, demonstrating a path of increasing responsibility and leadership  Demonstrated educational leadership and/or successful program management Recommended Qualifications: Experience working in a higher education environment Experience working with supporting quality education clinical experiences Experience developing and fostering school-university partnerships An understanding and/or experience with New Jersey teacher certification programs and requirements Experience working with dual enrollment programs Experience working with apprenticeship programs, DOL registered apprenticeship programs preferred.  Demonstrated data management, analysis, and application Demonstrated successful project management Personal Attributes and Traits: Effective written and oral communication skills Interest in and ability to work effectively with diverse groups of students, colleagues, and community members Attention to diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging  Commitment to supporting student success Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work collaboratively Self-reflective and responsive to constructive feedback. Starting Salary - AFT Range 22 - $69,373.45 - $79,781.83 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:  BENEFITS FOR PROFESSIONAL STAFF (AFT) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact  h umanresources@wpunj.edu . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Library--Evening-and-Weekend-Supervisor_R1015": {
      "title": "Library, Evening and Weekend Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-07\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  Job Summary The Evening and Weekends Supervisor position at Cheng Library requires a high degree of independence and initiative as well as temperament suited to providing impeccable service to the library’s' student, faculty, and community clients. Reporting to the Access Services Librarian, the Evening/Weekend supervisor oversees library operations in the evening and on weekends. The position is also responsible for the overall safety and security of the library building. Major Duties and Responsibilities     Supervises the staff of the Lending Services and Periodicals department during scheduled evening and weekend hours and arranges and oversees departmental coverage in the event of illness and other emergencies. Oversees aspects of the integrated library system, staffs the Lending Desk, and maintains borrower files. Aids Library users, including checking materials in and out, collecting fines, responding to inquiries for information in person, by phone, and email, and referring inquiries as needed. Supervises stack maintenance operations and trains personnel to sort, shelve, shelf read, shift, and other related operations. Addresses and resolves user concerns related to library policies, procedures, and services. Monitors and tracks all facility issues in coordination with other Lending Services personnel and maintains an accurate list of issues affecting the building and their specific locations and provides a summary of building conditions on a regular basis. Works closely with daytime student supervisor to train, supervise and monitor department’s student assistants. Serves as liaison to the Bursar’s office and is responsible for department accounting and daily receipts. Oversees various projects such as overdue notices, collection agency, database maintenance.  Prepares and maintains statistical reports for the department. Participates in library instruction as needed, teaching information literacy sessions. Other duties as needed and appropriate for the position.                                                                                                     Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree Minimum two years of experience in a library or another service-related field Competencies/Skills Required Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated customer service orientation. Ability to independently perform detailed, accurate work. Good computer skills. Familiarity with library systems and software, including spreadsheet software. Availability for the advertised time schedule. Flexibility to work extra hours on an as-needed basis. Other Information Sunday through Thursday 4pm to 12am (midnight) during the fall and spring semesters. Hours vary during the summer and between semesters. This description indicates the general nature and level of work performed by employees in the above job. It is not intended to be a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of employees assigned to the job. Starting Salary - AFT Range 24 - $66,067.40 - $75,985.55 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:  BENEFITS FOR PROFESSIONAL STAFF (AFT) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact  h umanresources@wpunj.edu . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Access-Services-Librarian_R1016-1": {
      "title": "Access Services Librarian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-07\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  Job Description Reporting to the Assistant Director for Access & Information Services, the Access Services Librarian plans, organizes, supervises, and coordinates services and staff for circulation, course reserves, stacks and related patron services. This position is a twelve-month tenure track position. PRINCIPAL RESPONSIBILITIES       Core: Plans, organizes, and coordinates the Library’s Lending Services staff for circulation, reserves, scanners, stacks and building maintenance, and related patron services. Provides supervision, training, and support for Lending Services staff including full-time and part-time staff and student assistants; works with relevant Library and University units in developing policies and procedures for circulation and related services. Develops and implements circulation, reserve, and copyright policies and procedures and communicates them to Library personnel and users. Collaborates with Information Systems, Registrar’s Office, Student Accounts, and other campus departments as appropriate to maintain accurate Banner database information; handles questions and concerns regarding Library policies and procedures as needed. Provides training and support for the integrated library system, including revisions of the policy file and circulation calendar. Generates management reports and prepares statistical reports. Maintains active awareness and knowledge of automated circulation processes, reciprocal borrowing, service enhancements, and copyright compliance. Performs routine administrative functions within Lending Services, including scheduling, and monitoring cash funds and reciprocal borrowing.       Other Duties: Stay up to date on new technologies, trends, and best practices in Access Services.  Participate in the general Reference Desk coverage rotation on weekdays and weekends, and in the User Education program. Participate in the Library’s Liaison Program with assignment to given departments as liaison and content selector. Serve on Library, University, regional and national committees as appropriate. Performing other duties as assigned and appropriate for the position. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS A master’s degree in the field of Library and Information Science (by time of appointment) - American Library Association (ALA) accredited. Second master’s degree required by time of application for tenure. One (1) year professional experience working in an automated environment with circulation and course reserves is required. Must possess excellent oral, written communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Experience working in an academic library and with diverse populations; knowledge of emerging technologies in Access Services. Experience working with an integrated library system or services platform.   Demonstrated commitment to service and professional development. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Supervisory experience. Second master’s degree preferred at time of appointment. PERSONAL ATTRIBUTES AND TRAITS Excellent verbal, written and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to effectively engage and communicate with diverse university communities and external audiences.  Demonstrated ability to prioritize work, set reasonable and attainable milestones, and stay on timeline to achieve agreed upon goals. Demonstrated ability to develop and sustain relationships with diverse groups including work colleagues, external clients, prospective students, employers’ representatives and community members. Able to stay motivated and effective when working independently. Evidence of working effectively in teams. This description indicates the general nature and level of work performed by employees in the above job. It is not intended to be a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of employees assigned to the job. Starting Salary - AFT Range 22 - $69,373.45 - $79,781.83 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:  BENEFITS FOR PROFESSIONAL STAFF (AFT) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact  h umanresources@wpunj.edu . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Collection-Development-and-Electronic-Resources-Librarian_R1017": {
      "title": "Collection Development and Electronic Resources Librarian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-07\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. William Paterson University is a purpose-driven, proudly diverse community—designated as both a public Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution—committed to creating transformative academic, professional, and personal experiences as a powerhouse of progress. We foster a workplace that values growth, flexibility, and community, and we are recognized as a 2024 and 2025 Forbes’ Best Employers by State, 2025 Great College to Work For, and honored with the NJBIZ Empowering Women Award .    Our 1,000 dedicated staff members enjoy competitive benefits, a four-day summer workweek, tuition support, and strong opportunities for internal promotion. Situated on a scenic suburban campus just 20 miles from New York City, WP offers a diverse, inclusive environment where your contributions fuel student success, economic and social mobility, and community engagement. Together, we empower our students through intentional, holistic support within flexible, innovative, and inclusive settings—preparing graduates to thrive professionally and personally, and to lead with a commitment to progress in New Jersey and beyond.  Job Description Reporting under the Resource Management Division of the Cheng Library, the Collection Development and Electronic Resources Librarian is responsible for the acquisition, maintenance, and management of the library's print and electronic collections, with a focus on institutional priorities and the needs of William Paterson University's library users. PRINCIPAL RESPONSIBILITIES Collection Development: Understanding the information needs of the library's users through surveys, feedback, and analysis of usage data to ensure collection development activities are consistent with the library's mission and user needs.  Identifying, selecting, and purchasing materials, including print and electronic resources from proprietary as well as open-source environments.  Managing collection development funds effectively.  Regularly evaluating the collection to identify gaps and needs and ensure the collection and accessible materials remain relevant and useful.  Coordinating the Library's weeding activities to ensure removal of outdated/irrelevant materials from the collection on a regular basis.  Electronic Resources: Negotiating and managing licenses for electronic resources.  Working with vendors to ensure access to electronic resources and addressing any emerging issues.  Analyzing usage statistics to assess the value of electronic resources and make informed decisions about subscriptions and renewals.  Working with IT staff and library systems personnel to ensure that electronic resources are accessible and functional.  Educating users on how to access and use electronic resources.  Participating in the Library User Education Program providing course-related instruction, orientations, demonstrations, and workshops.    Developing and maintaining instructional materials in print and digital formats—including LibGuides, tutorials, and other learning objects to assist patrons in developing information seeking skills. Other Duties: Working with other librarians and library staff to develop and maintain the collection.  Staying up to date on new technologies, trends, and best practices in collection development and electronic resources management.  Participating in the general Reference Desk coverage rotation on weekdays and weekends. Participating in the Library’s Liaison Program with assignment to given departments as liaison and content selector. Providing training to library staff on use of newly acquired/accessible resources and platforms.  Serving on Library, University, regional and national committees as appropriate. Performing other duties as assigned and appropriate for the position. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS A master’s degree in the field of Library and Information Science (by time of appointment) - American Library Association (ALA) accredited. Second master’s degree required by time of application for tenure. Knowledge of collection development policies, practices, and standards.  Familiarity with electronic resources, licensing, and vendor management.  Ability to evaluate information resources and assess their relevance and quality.  Proficiency in using library systems and software. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Second master’s degree preferred at time of appointment. PERSONAL ATTRIBUTES AND TRAITS Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to effectively engage and communicate with diverse university communities and external audiences.  Demonstrated ability to prioritize work, set reasonable and attainable milestones, and stay on timeline to achieve agreed upon goals. Demonstrated ability to develop and sustain relationships with diverse groups including work colleagues, external clients, prospective students, employers’ representatives and community members. Able to stay motivated and effective when working independently Evidence of working effectively in teams. This description indicates the general nature and level of work performed by employees in the above job. It is not intended to be a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of employees assigned to the job. Starting Salary - AFT Range 22 - $69,373.45 - $79,781.83 This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit:  BENEFITS FOR PROFESSIONAL STAFF (AFT) Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact  h umanresources@wpunj.edu . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Please see posting. Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
