ny maintenance or repair needs. Surface Disinfection: Regularly sanitize high touch surfaces such as doorknobs, handrails, light switches, and elevator buttons. Set up and Breakdown: Assist with the setup and breakdown of tables, chairs, and other equipment for events and meetings as needed. Reporting and Documentation: Report any maintenance or repair needs to the appropriate supervisor in a timely manner. Keep accurate records of cleaning activities and supplies used. Safety Compliance: Adhere to all safety protocols and guidelines, including the proper use and storage of cleaning chemicals and equipment. Report any safety hazards or incidents to the supervisor immediately. Team Collaboration: Collaborate with other custodial staff for consistent and efficient cleaning practices throughout the campus. Communicate effectively with supervisors and other team members regarding work schedules, tasks, and any issues or concerns. Customer Service: Provide friendly and helpful customer service to students, staff, and visitors. Respond to requests and inquiries in a professional and prompt manner. Requirements: Val id NJ driver's license required. High school diploma or equivalent. Previous custodial or cleaning experience preferred. Strong attention to detail and ability to follow instructions. Excellent time management skills and ability to prioritize tasks. Physical stamina to perform job duties such as lifting and moving furniture, walking, standing, and bending for extended periods. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Flexibility to work evening or weekend shifts as needed. Note: This is an IPFTE Union part-time position with an average of 20 hours per week. The schedule may vary and may include evenings and weekends. Rate of pay is $20.29/hour. Below is the link to the New Jersey residency requirement that career service employees are subject to: https://www.nj.gov/labor/research-info/njfirst.shtml This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health  and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please click on this link to our Benefits Package Pamphlet (CWA/IFPTE) Note: This is an ongoing posting designed to create a pool of qualified candidates for anticipated and future vacancies. An immediate opening may not be available at the time of application. Applicants who meet the qualifications may be contacted by the Hiring Manager if a position becomes available and they are selected to move forward in the interview process. Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and should be uploaded when prompted to upload your resume. General questions related to this application process, please contact humanresources@wpunj.edu  . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
