    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Adjunct-Faculty-Public-Relations-Integrated-Marketing-Communication_R334": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Public Relations-Integrated Marketing Communication",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-02\nPart time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. We invite you to join William Paterson University: a wonderful community to learn, work, grow, and thrive. William Paterson University has been named to Forbes’ prestigious “Best Employers by State” list for 2024, recognizing the institution as one of the best-ranked employers in New Jersey based on nationwide surveys. WP is one of four education institutions on the Garden State’s list this year. Here is the link to the article forbes-best-in-state-employers-new-jersey-2024. William Paterson University is among more than 40 companies and organizations that will be honored with a 2024 NJBIZ Empowering Women Award for their commitment to supporting and elevating women employees. William Paterson University employs approximately 1000 full time employees in the state who work in a variety of positions ranging from professors to administrative assistants and administrators, physical plant operations, campus police, athletics coaches, academic advisors, and more. William Paterson University supports a remote friendly hybrid work schedule for this role. William Paterson also boasts a four-day summer work week from mid-May to mid-August (Fridays off), during which all employees participate in our award-winning Summer Learning series. Spanning more than 400 wooded acres in suburban Wayne, New Jersey – just 20 miles from New York City – our campus is one of the most diverse in the nation and it ranks in the top 4 percent of colleges for social mobility. William Paterson is a strong proponent of employees growing their careers there. More than fifty percent of the University’s roles are filled by promotions from within. We’re not only committed to social mobility for our students, but also for our employees. Your work as a member of our team is important to our students and to the progress of our University. What you do here matters, and we value every contribution. Public Relations, Integrated Communication, Social Media, Strategic Writing The Department of Communication is seeking adjunct faculty members to develop and teach both undergraduate and graduate courses in our growing public relations/professional communication programs.  The Department is seeking candidates with professional public relations and/or integrated marketing communication experience.  Prior teaching experience is a plus.  A Master's degree (M.A., M.F.A. or M.B.A.) is required.     Areas of expertise should include some or all of the following:  integrated marketing communication, social/digital media management, multi-platform writing, advertising, crisis management, marketing and public relations. Candidates should be well-versed in the intersections between these areas. Teaching responsibilities may include the following courses: Integrated Communication, Social Media Management, Public Relations Management, Strategic Multi-Platform Writing and others as department need dictates.  Course sections may be during the day, night, weekends or online.     Candidates should possess a passion for public relations, an understanding of the integrated marketing communication mix and a dedication to helping students achieve in an increasingly complex and competitive professional environment.  Candidates should have a commitment to teaching diverse populations. Applicants :  please upload a cover letter, C.V. and samples /or links to their portfolio of professional work and/or teaching materials (syllabi, assignments, etc.).     ADJUNCTS PER CREDIT RATE: New employees - $2100/CREDIT Employees who have worked for 13+ semesters at WP - $2175/CREDIT This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health  and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit: https://www.wpunj.edu/human-resources/total-rewards/ Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to complete an application and submit a cover letter and resume/CV. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and all documents should be uploaded where prompted to upload your resume/cv. General questions related to this application process, please contact talent@wpunj.edu . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Adjunct-Faculty---Journalism_R441": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Journalism",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-02\nPart time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. We invite you to join William Paterson University: a wonderful community to learn, work, grow, and thrive. William Paterson University has been named to Forbes’ prestigious “Best Employers by State” list for 2024, recognizing the institution as one of the best-ranked employers in New Jersey based on nationwide surveys. WP is one of four education institutions on the Garden State’s list this year. Here is the link to the article forbes-best-in-state-employers-new-jersey-2024. William Paterson University is among more than 40 companies and organizations that will be honored with a 2024 NJBIZ Empowering Women Award for their commitment to supporting and elevating women employees. William Paterson University employs approximately 1000 full time employees in the state who work in a variety of positions ranging from professors to administrative assistants and administrators, physical plant operations, campus police, athletics coaches, academic advisors, and more. William Paterson University supports a remote friendly hybrid work schedule for this role. William Paterson also boasts a four-day summer work week from mid-May to mid-August (Fridays off), during which all employees participate in our award-winning Summer Learning series. Spanning more than 400 wooded acres in suburban Wayne, New Jersey – just 20 miles from New York City – our campus is one of the most diverse in the nation and it ranks in the top 4 percent of colleges for social mobility. William Paterson is a strong proponent of employees growing their careers there. More than fifty percent of the University’s roles are filled by promotions from within. We’re not only committed to social mobility for our students, but also for our employees. Your work as a member of our team is important to our students and to the progress of our University. What you do here matters, and we value every contribution. Journalism The Department of Communication is seeking adjunct faculty members to develop and teach undergraduate courses in our growing journalism program. The Department is seeking candidates with professional experience in journalism. Prior teaching experience is a plus. A master's degree (M.A., M.F.A. or M.B.A.) or commensurate professional experience is required.   Areas of expertise  should include some or all of the following: news reporting, news writing, feature writing, social/digital media management, and audio and television production. Candidates should be well versed in the intersections between these areas. Teaching responsibilities  may include the following courses: media law and ethics, news literacy, journalism, advanced reporting, journalism field studies, reporting through social media, press and the presidency, podcasting, mobile journalism, sports writing, journalism capstone, and others as department need dictates. Course sections may be during the day, night, or weekends, or online.   Candidates  should possess a passion for journalism, an understanding of the evolving news media landscape, and a dedication to helping students achieve in an increasingly complex and competitive professional environment. Candidates should have a commitment to teaching diverse populations. ADJUNCTS PER CREDIT RATE: New employees - $2100/CREDIT Employees who have worked for 13+ semesters at WP - $2175/CREDIT This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health  and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit: https://www.wpunj.edu/human-resources/total-rewards/ Invitation to apply Applicants :  please upload a cover letter, resume or CV, and samples and/or links to your portfolio of professional work and/or teaching materials (syllabi, assignments, etc.).  Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and should be uploaded when prompted to upload your resume. General questions related to this application process, please contact talent@wpunj.edu . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
    },
    "https://wpunj.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ext/job/William-Paterson-University/Adjunct-Faculty---Kinesiology_R274": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Kinesiology",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-02\nPart time\n\nThank you for your interest in working at William Paterson University. We invite you to join William Paterson University: a wonderful community to learn, work, grow, and thrive. William Paterson University has been named to Forbes’ prestigious “Best Employers by State” list for 2024, recognizing the institution as one of the best-ranked employers in New Jersey based on nationwide surveys. WP is one of four education institutions on the Garden State’s list this year. Here is the link to the article forbes-best-in-state-employers-new-jersey-2024. William Paterson University is among more than 40 companies and organizations that will be honored with a 2024 NJBIZ Empowering Women Award for their commitment to supporting and elevating women employees. William Paterson University employs approximately 1000 full time employees in the state who work in a variety of positions ranging from professors to administrative assistants and administrators, physical plant operations, campus police, athletics coaches, academic advisors, and more. William Paterson University supports a remote friendly hybrid work schedule for this role. William Paterson also boasts a four-day summer work week from mid-May to mid-August (Fridays off), during which all employees participate in our award-winning Summer Learning series. Spanning more than 400 wooded acres in suburban Wayne, New Jersey – just 20 miles from New York City – our campus is one of the most diverse in the nation and it ranks in the top 4 percent of colleges for social mobility. William Paterson is a strong proponent of employees growing their careers there. More than fifty percent of the University’s roles are filled by promotions from within. We’re not only committed to social mobility for our students, but also for our employees. Your work as a member of our team is important to our students and to the progress of our University. What you do here matters, and we value every contribution. William Paterson University invites applications for the position of Adjunct Faculty within the College of Science and Health, Department of Kinesiology. Thank you for expressing interest in serving as an adjunct faculty member at William Paterson University. Please note that there may not be a vacancy at this time. Rather, qualified applicants may be contacted if and when there is an immediate need, or on an exploratory basis for a future opening. Undergraduate courses in this department are taught both online and in person.  Below are the undergraduate majors in the Department of Kinesiology: Exercise Physiology Physical Education Teacher Certification Sport Management Sports Medicine Graduate courses in this department are taught both online and in person.  Below are the graduate majors in the Department of Kinesiology: Athletic Training Exercise Physiology Sport Administration Department Overview: The Department of Kinesiology provides the opportunity to earn degrees at the BA, BS, and MS level.  Students are prepared for a variety of careers including athletic training, exercise physiology, physical education, sport management/sport administration, and sports medicine.  Our students benefit from small classes, opportunities to conduct research, and internships at both local and out-of-state locations.  Kinesiology students also have access to state-of-the-art labs including the Human Performance Lab, the Human Motion Analysis Lab, and the Motor Behavior Lab. For more information about the department, please visit: https://www.wpunj.edu/cosh/departments/kinesiology/   Duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Using the course outline as a guide, develop relevant syllabi in order to deploy course content, objectives, and methods of student assessment. Contribute to student success by providing consistent and effective support and being available to the students for their questions and needs. Teach in person and/or online depending upon course schedules and department needs. Required Qualifications for Undergraduate courses: Masters in a relevant discipline to the Kinesiology undergraduate major; Exercise Physiology, Physical Education, Sport Management, and Sports Medicine. Full time or part-time employment in an area related to the Kinesiology undergraduate major. Preferred Qualifications: Professional certification and/or continuing professional education relevant to the kinesiology discipline. Experience teaching both online and in person courses. ------------------------------------  Required Qualifications for Graduate courses: Masters in a relevant discipline to the Kinesiology graduate major; Athletic Training, Exercise Physiology, and Sport Administration. Full time or part-time employment in an area related to the Kinesiology graduate major. Preferred Qualifications: Professional certification and/or continuing professional education relevant to the kinesiology discipline. Experience teaching both online and in person courses. Personal Attributes and Traits: Ability to translate kinesiology experience into pedagogical approaches that enhance curriculum relevance. Demonstrated commitment to engage in continuous professional development activities. Demonstrated commitment to content, teaching excellence, assessment strategies, and student success. Capable of exhibiting patience and resourcefulness in managing student challenges. Ability to effectively address competing wants and needs by developing and sustaining robust working relationships in a diverse environment. Demonstrated ability to set and work toward common goals in a collaborative environment. ADJUNCTS PER CREDIT RATE: New employees - $2100/CREDIT Employees who have worked for 13+ semesters at WP - $2175/CREDIT This position may be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health  and dental insurance and retirement plans. To learn more, please visit: https://www.wpunj.edu/human-resources/total-rewards/ Invitation to apply Interested candidates will be prompted to: Complete an application and submit a cover letter. Submission of all documents listed is required for consideration and should be uploaded when prompted to upload your resume. General questions related to this application process, please contact talent@wpunj.edu . Please include with your inquiry the Job Requisition number beginning with R as well as the job title and department. Salary Range: Total Rewards and Benefits: Click here to view the total rewards of working at WP William Paterson University is committed to protecting your privacy and will not sell your personal information. EEO Statement William Paterson University is dedicated to providing equal opportunities and equal access to all individuals regardless of race or ethnicity, sex/gender (including pregnancy), gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, civil union status, familial status, religion, national origin or citizenship, military service status, or any other category protected by law. William Paterson University does not discriminate on the basis of any category stated above or as prohibited by applicable law. Individuals from historically underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. For more information, visit University Facts"
